// `@generate` synthesizes against one concrete ClassInfo, so it does not apply to a generic template —
// `of`/`zero`, `Format`, `Equatable`/`Hashable` each say so. `Serialize`/`Deserialize` were the two
// kinds with NO arm, so they were accepted in silence: the type read as conforming, nothing synthesized
// the conformance, and the first `encode(v:)` died in the C compiler on a missing
// `_F<file>__Box_int32__as_Serialize` vtable symbol.
@generate(Serialize)
type value Box<T> {
    @field public T v;
    public ctor of(T v) { this.v = v; }
}
fn int32 main() {
    Box<int32> b = Box::<int32>.of(v: 42);
    return b.v;
}
